  "director_notes": "Revision of earth-ground-pound for Lisa's Sparkfall Ground Pound rework: no target (the cone is aimed by the caster's facing at the slam, destination 'point' marks the cone's far tip), castable while walking (the gather is an upper-body move), and a much bigger 9 m x 100 degree cone (footprint length 5 units = 9 m at Sparkfall's ~1.8 m character height). The new idea is the ground opening up: the fissures are a parallax-occlusion decal (style realistic, depth 1.0, exported with a height map) so they read as recessed slots with lit lips and dark walls from every camera, plus an additive 'cracks' decal that glows amber only at the bottom of the cracks and cools over ~3 s. Marks linger 4.8 s at full strength and fade over 1.6 s. Timeline: gather 0-600, hang 600-680, slam 680-760, rupture 720-1500 (six rows, row_delay 130, growth 1.1), climax 1400-1850 at the tip, linger 1800-4800 (seeping dust, trickling grit, quiet crackle), close 4800-6400. Sound: rumble -> whoosh -> impact + boom -> crack + crash every 140 ms over a rumble -> deep boom + crash -> quiet crackle and rumble. In Unity: URP decal projector with a custom parallax-occlusion decal shader (albedo, height, normal, emissive), Blender rock meshes for spikes and debris, dust as a world-space particle system.",
